<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=snowshoe">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Snowshoe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3800–3700 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Snowshoes are footwear with a large footprint that spreads the wearer's weight so that the wearer travels largely on top of snow. Historians believe they were invented 4,000 to 6,000 years ago, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. The oldest snowshoe known, a crude frame found in a melting glacier in the Dolomites in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 2016, dates to between 3800 and 3700 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> wrote that the inhabitants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> bound flat surfaces of leather or round wooden blocks under their feet. The webbed snowshoe of rawhide lattice on a hardwood frame came from Indigenous peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a> described those of the Huron and Algonquin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/snowshoe.jpg" alt="Snowshoe" width="330" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Another one of my pictures: This photograph was taken by Medium69 (William Crochot) and released under the license stated below. You are fre · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raquettes_à_neige_-_20150802_13h01_(10683).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 3800 to 3700 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Dolomites, Italy</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Historians believe snowshoes were invented 4,000 to 6,000 years ago, probably in Central Asia. Jacqui Wood has suggested that the Chalcolithic mummy Ötzi's equipment, read as a backpack frame, was part of a snowshoe.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=snowshoe">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
